    "label": "23",
    "prompt": "",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p24-q23-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Show that $\\frac{x^2+x}{x^2+4x+3}$ can be written as $\\frac{x}{x+a}$ where $a$ is a positive integer.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac{x^2+x}{x^2+4x+3}=\\frac{x(x+1)}{(x+1)(x+3)}=\\frac{x}{x+3}$, so $a=3$, with $x\\ne-1,-3$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{x^2+x}{x^2+4x+3}&=\\frac{x(x+1)}{(x+1)(x+3)}\\\\&=\\frac{x}{x+3}\\end{align*}$$\nThus $a=3$. The original denominator excludes $x=-1$ and $x=-3$; these restrictions remain after cancellation.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 24
      },
      {
        "id": "p24-q23-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Hence, given $f(x)=\\frac{x^2+x}{x^2+4x+3}$, find an expression for $f^{-1}(x)$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$f^{-1}(x)=\\frac{3x}{1-x}$, $x\\ne1,-\\frac12$. Use $f(x)=\\frac{x}{x+3}$ and interchange $x$ and $y$.",
          "worked": "Using part a, write $y=\\frac{x}{x+3}$ and interchange $x$ and $y$.\n$$\\begin{align*}x&=\\frac{y}{y+3}\\\\x(y+3)&=y\\\\xy+3x&=y\\\\3x&=y(1-x)\\\\y&=\\frac{3x}{1-x}\\\\f^{-1}(x)&=\\frac{3x}{1-x}\\end{align*}$$\nThe original function has domain $\\mathbb R\\setminus\\{-3,-1\\}$ and range $\\mathbb R\\setminus\\{1,-\\frac12\\}$. Hence the inverse has domain $\\mathbb R\\setminus\\{1,-\\frac12\\}$ and range $\\mathbb R\\setminus\\{-3,-1\\}$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 60
      }
    ]
  },
